1
00:00:05,790 --> 00:00:07,460
Okay.

2
00:00:05,790 --> 00:00:07,460
Aah.

3
00:00:08,290 --> 00:00:12,260
Listen, I'm gonna be moving out, so you are gonna be in charge of paying the rent.

4
00:00:12,420 --> 00:00:14,510
Right, and when is that due?

5
00:00:12,420 --> 00:00:14,510
First of the month.

6
00:00:14,680 --> 00:00:16,220
And that's every month?

7
00:00:16,890 --> 00:00:19,100
No, just the months you actually want to live here.

8
00:00:19,260 --> 00:00:20,510
Ah.

9
00:00:20,680 --> 00:00:22,890
Okay, here's the phone bill.

10
00:00:23,890 --> 00:00:25,890
Oh, my God!

11
00:00:26,690 --> 00:00:28,520
That's our phone number.

12
00:00:29,980 --> 00:00:33,400
Look, I know I kind of sprung this whole me-moving-out-on-you thing.

13
00:00:33,570 --> 00:00:36,990
So why don't I just cover you for a while?

14
00:00:33,570 --> 00:00:36,990
No, no. No way.

15
00:00:37,160 --> 00:00:40,830
Joey Tribbiani does not take charity...

16
00:00:41,120 --> 00:00:42,620
anymore.

17
00:00:42,870 --> 00:00:45,960
It's not charity, Joe.

18
00:00:42,870 --> 00:00:45,960
No, forget it.

19
00:00:46,120 --> 00:00:48,670
Okay? I mean, thanks, but I'm done taking money from you.

20
00:00:48,840 --> 00:00:51,380
All right? I can take care of myself. Now, what's next? Come on.

21
00:00:51,550 --> 00:00:53,590
Okay, uh, here's the electric bill.

22
00:00:53,760 --> 00:00:56,470
This is how much we pay for electric?

23
00:00:53,760 --> 00:00:56,470
Well, yeah.

24
00:01:01,220 --> 00:01:03,930
So we'll do the rest of the bills later, then?

25
00:01:43,680 --> 00:01:45,680
So is Joey gonna have to give up the apartment?

26
00:01:45,850 --> 00:01:48,560
I hope not. I tried to offer him money, but he wouldn't take it.

27
00:01:48,730 --> 00:01:50,190
How much do you think he needs?

28
00:01:50,360 --> 00:01:53,070
I figure $1500 would cover him for a few months, you know...

29
00:01:53,230 --> 00:01:56,240
but I have to trick him into taking it so I don't hurt his pride.

30
00:01:56,400 --> 00:01:59,150
Yeah. Well, why don't you hire him as an actor?

31
00:02:00,410 --> 00:02:04,450
You could have him dress up and put on little skits whenever you want.

32
00:02:06,370 --> 00:02:08,870
Well, that would help the pride thing.

33
00:02:10,210 --> 00:02:11,380
Hey.

34
00:02:10,210 --> 00:02:11,380
Hey.

35
00:02:11,540 --> 00:02:14,590
Wow, you look great. Do you wanna move in with me tomorrow?

36
00:02:15,880 --> 00:02:17,630
Okay.

37
00:02:15,880 --> 00:02:17,630
Okay.

38
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:20,470
What do you girls have planned for tonight?

39
00:02:20,640 --> 00:02:23,390
Instead of being sad that tonight's my last night with Rachel...

40
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:25,390
we thought we'd go out and celebrate:

41
00:02:25,560 --> 00:02:27,220
Rachel's moving in with Phoebe.

42
00:02:27,390 --> 00:02:30,600
And also my birthday. Ha, ha.

43
00:02:27,390 --> 00:02:30,600
It's not your birthday.

44
00:02:31,310 --> 00:02:32,860
What a mean thing to say.

45
00:02:33,020 --> 00:02:36,150
I would never tell you it was not your birthday.

46
00:02:37,110 --> 00:02:38,400
Hey.

47
00:02:37,110 --> 00:02:38,400
Hey.

48
00:02:38,570 --> 00:02:42,030
Hey, so you guys have anything planned for the big last night?

49
00:02:42,200 --> 00:02:45,950
Well, instead of just hanging out, we figure we'd do nothing.

50
00:02:46,910 --> 00:02:49,450
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Knicks' season opener tonight.

51
00:02:49,910 --> 00:02:52,120
I thought maybe you guys would come and watch it.

52
00:02:52,290 --> 00:02:53,830
I don't know, Ross.

53
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:56,250
Not if you talk about how you gave up basketball...

54
00:02:56,420 --> 00:02:57,880
to become a paleontologist.

55
00:02:58,050 --> 00:03:02,630
I did give up a career in basketball to become a paleontologist.

56
00:03:03,470 --> 00:03:05,640
Pheebs, I was wondering...

57
00:03:03,470 --> 00:03:05,640
You're not dressed yet?

58
00:03:05,930 --> 00:03:08,600
We're supposed to start having fun in 15 minutes!

59
00:03:09,640 --> 00:03:12,600
Well, and clearly, not a minute sooner.

60
00:03:13,400 --> 00:03:16,940
Rachel, you are packed, though, right? I mean, please tell me you're packed.

61
00:03:17,110 --> 00:03:20,440
Of course I'm packed. Monica, relax.

62
00:03:20,610 --> 00:03:23,070
I wanted to ask Phoebe for her opinion on what I should wear.

63
00:03:23,240 --> 00:03:25,820
My God, I cannot get a minute of peace.

64
00:03:29,620 --> 00:03:31,660
Oh, my God.

65
00:03:33,500 --> 00:03:35,750
Monica's just gonna kill you.

66
00:03:36,090 --> 00:03:37,130
I know.

67
00:03:37,300 --> 00:03:39,460
What you're wearing is fine for that.

68
00:03:41,050 --> 00:03:42,660
Rachel, I want to borrow

69
00:03:43,970 --> 00:03:45,840
You're not packed!

70
00:03:46,010 --> 00:03:48,430
You're not packed even a little bit.

71
00:03:49,470 --> 00:03:50,810
Surprise.

72
00:03:52,940 --> 00:03:54,980
Don't get mad, because, look, this is what happened.

73
00:03:55,150 --> 00:03:59,020
So I started packing, and then I realized, "What am I doing?"

74
00:03:59,190 --> 00:04:02,070
I am lousy at packing, right?

75
00:04:02,240 --> 00:04:03,820
But you love packing.

76
00:04:03,990 --> 00:04:08,030
So as a gift to you on our last night...

77
00:04:08,700 --> 00:04:10,240
Ta-da.

78
00:04:12,830 --> 00:04:14,500
I'll be coordinator.

79
00:04:14,670 --> 00:04:16,830
Oh, my God, I'm so sorry. I didn't get you anything.

80
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:18,170
Oh.

81
00:04:18,630 --> 00:04:21,170
Look, everybody has to help. Phoebe, you can help, can't you?

82
00:04:21,340 --> 00:04:22,710
I have plans.

83
00:04:23,260 --> 00:04:25,630
You have plans with us.

84
00:04:23,260 --> 00:04:25,630
That's right.

85
00:04:26,340 --> 00:04:30,260
All right. Chandler can make boxes, Ross can wrap, and Joey can lift things.

86
00:04:30,430 --> 00:04:32,390
Tell the guys they have to help out.

87
00:04:30,430 --> 00:04:32,390
Okay.

88
00:04:32,560 --> 00:04:34,850
Okay.

89
00:04:32,560 --> 00:04:34,850
My God, thank you.

90
00:04:35,810 --> 00:04:38,860
Hurry! Monica's gonna make you pack. She's got jobs for everyone.

91
00:04:39,020 --> 00:04:41,690
Now, it's too late for me, but save yourselves.

92
00:04:42,990 --> 00:04:44,030
Okay.

93
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:47,570
The movers will be here in 11 hours. Rachel has not packed.

94
00:04:47,740 --> 00:04:49,700
Now, everybody has to help. Chandler...

95
00:04:49,870 --> 00:04:52,370
No, I have plans with Joey.

96
00:04:52,540 --> 00:04:56,540
I thought you said you were doing nothing.

97
00:04:52,540 --> 00:04:56,540
Yes, but for the last time.

98
00:04:58,380 --> 00:04:59,790
Okay, fine. Now, Ross...

99
00:04:59,960 --> 00:05:02,380
Oh, but I can't do it.

100
00:04:59,960 --> 00:05:02,380
Why not?

101
00:05:02,550 --> 00:05:06,170
Don't you have Ben?

102
00:05:02,550 --> 00:05:06,170
Because I have Ben.

103
00:05:07,180 --> 00:05:09,760
It's almost 8:00, it's almost past his bedtime. Where is he?

104
00:05:09,930 --> 00:05:11,390
He's at a dinner party.

105
00:05:13,850 --> 00:05:16,560
Is he really coming? Because I can see into your apartment.

106
00:05:16,730 --> 00:05:19,150
Of course he is. Uh, what?

107
00:05:19,310 --> 00:05:21,730
You think I'd just use my son as an excuse?

108
00:05:21,900 --> 00:05:24,360
What kind of father do you think I am?

109
00:05:25,030 --> 00:05:26,110
All right. Sorry.

110
00:05:27,320 --> 00:05:29,660
I gotta go make a fake Ben.

111
00:05:34,040 --> 00:05:37,710
Here it is. Our last pizzas together as roommates.

112
00:05:37,870 --> 00:05:40,380
I wish I'd known you were gonna do that. I ordered Chinese.

113
00:05:40,540 --> 00:05:41,880
Oh. Oh, that's okay.

114
00:05:42,050 --> 00:05:44,920
Hey, actually, in a way it's kind of nice. You know?

115
00:05:45,090 --> 00:05:49,220
Our last dinner together. Me, bringing the food of my ancestors...

116
00:05:49,390 --> 00:05:51,470
you, the food of yours.

117
00:05:54,100 --> 00:05:55,600
Huh?

118
00:05:56,230 --> 00:05:59,100
Say, Joe, I had a strange idea for what to do on our last night.

119
00:05:59,270 --> 00:06:02,110
What do you say we play a little, uh, foosball for money?

120
00:06:02,270 --> 00:06:06,360
Are you crazy? You haven't beaten me once since my injury

121
00:06:02,270 --> 00:06:06,360
plagued '97 season.

122
00:06:06,530 --> 00:06:08,530
It'd be easier if you'd just give me your money.

123
00:06:08,700 --> 00:06:10,110
Yes, it would.

124
00:06:11,120 --> 00:06:13,330
Ahem. What do you say to $50?

125
00:06:13,490 --> 00:06:15,620
Okay, you're on.

126
00:06:13,490 --> 00:06:15,620
Okay, let's play.

127
00:06:15,790 --> 00:06:17,910
The big game. Italy versus...

128
00:06:18,080 --> 00:06:19,540
China, apparently.

129
00:06:22,130 --> 00:06:25,800
Oh, look, it's the Rollerblades.

130
00:06:25,960 --> 00:06:27,920
Oh, God.

131
00:06:28,090 --> 00:06:30,630
You remember when we got these?

132
00:06:31,430 --> 00:06:32,840
No.

133
00:06:34,010 --> 00:06:35,600
Oh, I guess you weren't there.

134
00:06:37,310 --> 00:06:40,230
You guys, we said we were gonna have fun.

135
00:06:40,400 --> 00:06:43,230
Come on. Hey, ha, ha, remember the time?

136
00:06:48,530 --> 00:06:49,990
You don't remember?

137
00:06:51,070 --> 00:06:54,490
Sorry, Pheebs. I guess I'm just really sad that I'm leaving.

138
00:06:54,660 --> 00:06:56,620
I'm gonna miss you so much.

139
00:06:56,790 --> 00:07:00,290
Well, this doesn't have to be so sad though, you know?

140
00:07:00,460 --> 00:07:03,420
Instead of thinking about how much you're gonna miss about each other...

141
00:07:03,580 --> 00:07:06,920
you should, like, think about some of the things you're not gonna miss.

142
00:07:08,340 --> 00:07:10,340
I don't think there's anything.

143
00:07:10,510 --> 00:07:12,550
Come on, there's gotta be something.

144
00:07:12,720 --> 00:07:15,300
Nope. She's perfect.

145
00:07:18,890 --> 00:07:20,180
I have one.

146
00:07:21,310 --> 00:07:23,770
Good. Great. Okay, you can go first.

147
00:07:23,940 --> 00:07:26,400
Uh, well, I guess I'm not gonna miss the fact...

148
00:07:26,570 --> 00:07:30,570
that you're never allowed to move the phone pen. Ha, ha.

149
00:07:34,200 --> 00:07:36,530
That's a good one. Okay, Monica, anything?

150
00:07:36,700 --> 00:07:39,290
You know, does Rachel move the phone pen?

151
00:07:40,540 --> 00:07:42,620
Aw, sometimes.

152
00:07:40,540 --> 00:07:42,620
Ha, ha.

153
00:07:43,170 --> 00:07:44,710
Always, actually.

154
00:07:46,590 --> 00:07:48,920
Good. There you go. Doesn't everyone feel better?

155
00:07:50,550 --> 00:07:52,550
It's not just the phone pen.

156
00:07:53,510 --> 00:07:55,720
It's just that I never get my messages.

157
00:07:56,140 --> 00:07:57,550
You get your messages.

158
00:07:57,720 --> 00:08:01,220
Well, I don't think it counts if you have to read them off your hand...

159
00:08:01,390 --> 00:08:04,060
after you've fallen asleep on the couch.

160
00:08:04,230 --> 00:08:06,900
So you missed a message from who? Chandler?

161
00:08:07,060 --> 00:08:08,730
Or your mom?

162
00:08:09,280 --> 00:08:10,610
Or Chandler?

163
00:08:10,780 --> 00:08:12,070
Or your mom?

164
00:08:16,120 --> 00:08:18,950
Great, it worked. No one's sad. Heh.

165
00:08:20,950 --> 00:08:22,120
Yes.

166
00:08:20,950 --> 00:08:22,120
Ah.

167
00:08:22,290 --> 00:08:26,250
I win again. Ha, ha, that's, like, 500 bucks you owe me. Woo

168
00:08:22,290 --> 00:08:26,250
hoo!

169
00:08:26,750 --> 00:08:28,460
Man. Five hundred dollars.

170
00:08:28,630 --> 00:08:33,170
That is a lot of electricity, huh? Woo

171
00:08:28,630 --> 00:08:33,170
hoo!

172
00:08:33,340 --> 00:08:35,680
Ooh, I gotta buy some food.

173
00:08:35,840 --> 00:08:38,890
Okay, okay. Give me a chance to win my money back. Sudden death...

174
00:08:39,060 --> 00:08:41,720
one goal, $1000.

175
00:08:42,310 --> 00:08:43,770
You serious?

176
00:08:42,310 --> 00:08:43,770
Oh, yes.

177
00:08:44,310 --> 00:08:45,440
Okay.

178
00:08:45,600 --> 00:08:47,480
Get ready to owe me.

179
00:08:45,600 --> 00:08:47,480
Okay.

180
00:08:47,650 --> 00:08:48,940
Okay, here we go. Ready?

181
00:09:13,760 --> 00:09:15,470
No, no, no!

182
00:09:13,760 --> 00:09:15,470
No, no, no!

183
00:09:15,630 --> 00:09:18,970
No one can beat me.

184
00:09:22,810 --> 00:09:26,560
See, now that's why only the little fake men are supposed to do the kicking.

185
00:09:31,320 --> 00:09:32,650
Hello?

186
00:09:32,820 --> 00:09:35,650
Oh, hi, Ross. See, other people call me.

187
00:09:35,820 --> 00:09:38,570
Ooh, your brother. Score.

188
00:09:40,070 --> 00:09:42,910
What's up?

189
00:09:40,070 --> 00:09:42,910
I'm here with Ben.

190
00:09:43,080 --> 00:09:44,740
Thought we'd say hi.

191
00:09:44,910 --> 00:09:48,750
Put him on.

192
00:09:44,910 --> 00:09:48,750
Ben, say hi to Aunt Monica.

193
00:09:50,380 --> 00:09:53,000
Oh, I guess he doesn't feel like talking right now.

194
00:09:53,170 --> 00:09:56,670
Uh, he's smiling, though.

195
00:09:57,340 --> 00:10:00,010
Okay, talk to you later.

196
00:10:06,680 --> 00:10:09,310
I think it was better when you guys were sad.

197
00:10:09,480 --> 00:10:12,980
Hey, oh, remember the Rollerblades? Oh.

198
00:10:14,820 --> 00:10:17,320
You know what else I'm not gonna miss? "I'm Monica.

199
00:10:17,490 --> 00:10:20,860
I wash the toilets 17 times a day, even if people are on it."

200
00:10:22,160 --> 00:10:24,950
"Hi, I'm Rachel. Is my sweater too tight? No?

201
00:10:25,120 --> 00:10:27,540
Oh, I'd better wash it and shrink it."

202
00:10:28,410 --> 00:10:31,960
"I'm Monica. I don't get phone messages from interesting people. Ever."

203
00:10:32,130 --> 00:10:33,630
Hey, I call her.

204
00:10:34,840 --> 00:10:40,380
"Oh, my God. I love Ross. I hate Ross. I love Ross. I hate Ross."

205
00:10:41,300 --> 00:10:43,090
"Oh, my God. I can't find a boyfriend.

206
00:10:43,350 --> 00:10:45,030
So I guess I'll just stumble across the hall

207
00:10:45,030 --> 00:10:47,520
and sleep with the first guy I find in there."

208
00:10:53,230 --> 00:10:57,400
Yeah, we should get a move on if we want to make those dinner reservations.

209
00:11:04,200 --> 00:11:05,740
Still broken?

210
00:11:06,410 --> 00:11:08,040
It sucks, man.

211
00:11:08,200 --> 00:11:11,040
Your last night here, and I lose the two most important things:

212
00:11:11,210 --> 00:11:13,500
The foosball table...

213
00:11:13,670 --> 00:11:15,500
and $500.

214
00:11:16,710 --> 00:11:19,380
Well, you know, there are other ways you can win back your money.

215
00:11:19,550 --> 00:11:22,180
How about blackjack?

216
00:11:19,550 --> 00:11:22,180
Ah, not my game.

217
00:11:22,340 --> 00:11:24,800
Okay, uh, you know what? We can play a new game.

218
00:11:24,970 --> 00:11:27,350
A new game. It's fun.

219
00:11:24,970 --> 00:11:27,350
What's it called?

220
00:11:28,770 --> 00:11:30,230
Cups.

221
00:11:31,770 --> 00:11:35,230
I don't know how to play Cups.

222
00:11:31,770 --> 00:11:35,230
I'll teach you. It's really easy and fun.

223
00:11:35,400 --> 00:11:37,520
All right.

224
00:11:35,400 --> 00:11:37,520
Okay, here you go.

225
00:11:38,860 --> 00:11:40,780
I have two queens. What do you have?

226
00:11:41,280 --> 00:11:43,530
A two and a five.

227
00:11:41,280 --> 00:11:43,530
Whoa, you win. Fifty dollars.

228
00:11:46,450 --> 00:11:48,790
Really?

229
00:11:46,450 --> 00:11:48,790
Oh, yeah. Okay, let's play again. Ready?

230
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:54,290
What have you got?

231
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:54,290
A four and a nine.

232
00:11:54,920 --> 00:11:56,460
You're kidding, right?

233
00:11:57,630 --> 00:12:00,340
No. Why?

234
00:11:57,630 --> 00:12:00,340
Well, that's a full cup.

235
00:12:02,130 --> 00:12:04,550
Damn, I am good at Cups.

236
00:12:06,550 --> 00:12:08,260
I'm not talking to her.

237
00:12:08,430 --> 00:12:10,350
One of you has to take the first step...

238
00:12:10,520 --> 00:12:12,890
and it should be you because she's the one who's leaving.

239
00:12:13,060 --> 00:12:14,770
It's harder for her.

240
00:12:16,020 --> 00:12:17,230
Maybe you're right.

241
00:12:17,480 --> 00:12:19,940
But she made fun of my phone pen.

242
00:12:20,690 --> 00:12:22,860
I know. I took it hard too.

243
00:12:26,620 --> 00:12:28,990
Listen, Rachel, I feel bad about what happened...

244
00:12:29,160 --> 00:12:31,660
What are you doing?

245
00:12:29,160 --> 00:12:31,660
I'm unpacking.

246
00:12:31,830 --> 00:12:35,790
What?

247
00:12:31,830 --> 00:12:35,790
I'm not moving. Is that picture straight?

248
00:12:35,960 --> 00:12:38,790
It needs to go about 20 blocks to the left.

249
00:12:38,960 --> 00:12:40,130
Hey, you know what?

250
00:12:40,300 --> 00:12:43,170
You're the one who wants this big change and move in with Chandler.

251
00:12:43,340 --> 00:12:45,300
You should go. Why do I have to leave?

252
00:12:45,470 --> 00:12:49,220
Because It's my apartment!

253
00:12:45,470 --> 00:12:49,220
Well, it's mine too. What else you got?

254
00:12:50,470 --> 00:12:52,100
How about: You're moving!

255
00:12:53,480 --> 00:12:55,850
No, no, no.

256
00:12:53,480 --> 00:12:55,850
Yes, yes, yes.

257
00:12:58,900 --> 00:13:00,480
Okay, Monica...

258
00:13:02,860 --> 00:13:04,280
This is ridiculous.

259
00:13:06,200 --> 00:13:07,860
We should be packing you.

260
00:13:09,830 --> 00:13:12,870
Hey, how you guys doing?

261
00:13:09,830 --> 00:13:12,870
Great. Monica's moving.

262
00:13:14,370 --> 00:13:15,460
I am not!

263
00:13:15,620 --> 00:13:18,670
Oh, really? Well, how come all your stuff is in this box?

264
00:13:18,830 --> 00:13:22,250
Okay, you guys, you guys, I think I know what's going on here.

265
00:13:22,420 --> 00:13:25,050
Okay? You guys? Stop!

266
00:13:25,760 --> 00:13:30,430
I know that you're acting mad because you think that will make it easier to leave.

267
00:13:30,600 --> 00:13:33,680
But deep down, you're still really sad. Deep, deep down.

268
00:13:33,850 --> 00:13:36,100
No, Phoebe, I am mad!

269
00:13:33,850 --> 00:13:36,100
Well, deep, deep, deep down.

270
00:13:36,270 --> 00:13:37,730
Yeah, I'm just mad.

271
00:13:38,560 --> 00:13:39,690
Then keep running.

272
00:13:43,110 --> 00:13:44,190
You win.

273
00:13:44,360 --> 00:13:46,990
What did you have?

274
00:13:44,360 --> 00:13:46,990
Doesn't matter. Nothing beats...

275
00:13:47,150 --> 00:13:49,490
a three and a six.

276
00:13:49,660 --> 00:13:51,870
That, my friend, is "D Cup."

277
00:13:54,040 --> 00:13:56,410
Okay, now, how much have you won so far?

278
00:13:57,080 --> 00:14:00,080
Wow. Seven hundred.

279
00:13:57,080 --> 00:14:00,080
Not 700 exactly?

280
00:14:00,420 --> 00:14:02,710
Yeah.

281
00:14:00,420 --> 00:14:02,710
Heh. Double it.

282
00:14:04,050 --> 00:14:06,920
What?

283
00:14:04,050 --> 00:14:06,920
Yeah, see, in Cups, once you get $700...

284
00:14:07,090 --> 00:14:08,220
you have to double it.

285
00:14:09,390 --> 00:14:11,930
Really?

286
00:14:09,390 --> 00:14:11,930
Hey, I didn't make up the rules.

287
00:14:13,350 --> 00:14:18,180
Okay, so now, after you receive the doubling bonus, you get, uh, one card.

288
00:14:18,350 --> 00:14:22,860
Now, that one card could be worth $100, which brings your total to 1500.

289
00:14:23,020 --> 00:14:24,360
Ooh.

290
00:14:23,020 --> 00:14:24,360
No, no, no.

291
00:14:24,530 --> 00:14:28,780
Don't get too excited, because that's not gonna happen unless you get the... No way.

292
00:14:31,820 --> 00:14:34,030
Well, this is the last box of your clothes.

293
00:14:34,200 --> 00:14:37,160
I'm just gonna label it "What were you thinking?"

294
00:14:38,620 --> 00:14:42,210
Funny, I was just gonna go across the hall and write that on Chandler.

295
00:14:44,840 --> 00:14:47,920
Okay, you guys, I don't mean to make things worse, but...

296
00:14:48,090 --> 00:14:50,220
I don't wanna live with Rachel anymore.

297
00:14:50,380 --> 00:14:52,970
What?

298
00:14:50,380 --> 00:14:52,970
You're just so mean to each other.

299
00:14:53,140 --> 00:14:56,430
And I don't wanna end up like that with Rachel. I still like you.

300
00:14:57,140 --> 00:14:59,640
Well, Phoebe, that's fine because I'm not moving.

301
00:14:59,810 --> 00:15:02,940
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Phoebe, you gotta take her.

302
00:15:03,690 --> 00:15:05,400
You know, I know I said some bad stuff...

303
00:15:05,570 --> 00:15:08,740
but Rachel does have some qualities that make her a good roommate.

304
00:15:08,900 --> 00:15:10,360
Oh, really? Like what, Monica?

305
00:15:13,490 --> 00:15:15,950
You know how she has 147,000 pair of boots?

306
00:15:16,120 --> 00:15:17,790
Oh, yeah, good start, Mon.

307
00:15:18,870 --> 00:15:21,000
She lets you borrow them.

308
00:15:18,870 --> 00:15:21,000
Yeah.

309
00:15:21,170 --> 00:15:23,880
And you stretch them out with your big old clown feet.

310
00:15:25,500 --> 00:15:28,250
Do you wanna live outside? Because it's getting cold.

311
00:15:30,090 --> 00:15:31,300
She gets tons of catalogs...

312
00:15:31,470 --> 00:15:35,010
and, um, she'll fold down the pages of the things she thinks I'd like.

313
00:15:35,390 --> 00:15:37,850
What else?

314
00:15:35,390 --> 00:15:37,850
Uh...

315
00:15:38,020 --> 00:15:39,970
When I take a shower...

316
00:15:40,350 --> 00:15:42,480
she leaves me little notes on the mirror.

317
00:15:42,650 --> 00:15:44,900
Yeah, I do. I do do that.

318
00:15:45,060 --> 00:15:49,150
That's nice. I like having things to read in the bathroom.

319
00:15:51,360 --> 00:15:53,820
When I fall asleep on the couch after reading...

320
00:15:55,200 --> 00:15:57,030
she covers me over with a blanket.

321
00:15:57,410 --> 00:16:01,160
Well, you know, I don't want you to be cold.

322
00:16:04,540 --> 00:16:07,500
And when I told her I was gonna be moving in with Chandler...

323
00:16:08,500 --> 00:16:10,340
she was really supportive.

324
00:16:13,050 --> 00:16:14,760
You were so great.

325
00:16:16,140 --> 00:16:18,850
You made it so easy.

326
00:16:20,270 --> 00:16:22,640
And now you have to leave.

327
00:16:23,060 --> 00:16:25,520
And I have to live with a boy!

328
00:16:28,570 --> 00:16:30,570
It's gonna be fine.

329
00:16:31,610 --> 00:16:34,570
Okay, Rachel. Now I can't wait to live with you.

330
00:16:35,070 --> 00:16:36,200
You know what we should do?

331
00:16:36,370 --> 00:16:38,740
Bring Monica, and then we can all live there together.

332
00:16:38,910 --> 00:16:40,410
We'll have so much fun!

333
00:16:42,080 --> 00:16:44,290
But, honey, I think she's moving in with Chandler.

334
00:16:44,460 --> 00:16:46,000
Oh, that's right.

335
00:16:46,540 --> 00:16:47,630
You're still set on that?

336
00:16:49,210 --> 00:16:50,840
Kind of.

337
00:16:56,800 --> 00:16:58,050
Oh, my God.

338
00:17:01,560 --> 00:17:03,430
Hello? Hey, Mon.

339
00:17:03,600 --> 00:17:05,810
How's the packing going?

340
00:17:05,980 --> 00:17:09,730
Ben? He's fine. Yeah, he's right... Oh, my God.

341
00:17:11,110 --> 00:17:14,440
Get your head out of your shirt there, son.

342
00:17:14,740 --> 00:17:16,030
What?

343
00:17:16,280 --> 00:17:19,320
Yeah, it's a pumpkin. I'll come pack.

344
00:17:22,410 --> 00:17:23,700
Hey.

345
00:17:23,870 --> 00:17:26,210
What's wrong?

346
00:17:23,870 --> 00:17:26,210
Ross and I were helping the girls pack...

347
00:17:26,370 --> 00:17:30,330
took a little break. I lost $1500 to him in Cups.

348
00:17:31,630 --> 00:17:35,010
Wha...? How did you lose at Cups?

349
00:17:35,170 --> 00:17:36,720
The same way you lost.

350
00:17:36,880 --> 00:17:41,260
I started out with the king and the queen. Bam. Ross gets a two and a three.

351
00:17:41,850 --> 00:17:45,220
Then I get a jack and a king. Boom. Ross gets a four and five.

352
00:17:45,810 --> 00:17:48,640
Even Ross was getting the Cup card, the D Cup...

353
00:17:48,810 --> 00:17:54,070
the sitting

354
00:17:48,810 --> 00:17:54,070
down bonus. Meanwhile, I didn't even get a half cup. Nothing.

355
00:17:54,740 --> 00:17:55,940
Oh, man.

356
00:17:56,700 --> 00:17:58,200
He never played before either.

357
00:17:58,360 --> 00:18:02,280
You know what I think? I think beginner's luck, very important in Cups.

358
00:18:03,540 --> 00:18:05,790
Let's just play one more hand. One more hand.

359
00:18:05,950 --> 00:18:09,710
No, no more. I cannot lose another dime. I'm serious this time.

360
00:18:09,880 --> 00:18:13,290
In fact, look. There's... I wanna give you something, okay?

361
00:18:13,460 --> 00:18:16,300
And let me give it to you now before I pawn it for Cups money.

362
00:18:18,510 --> 00:18:22,180
Now, I want you to have the big, white dog...

363
00:18:22,350 --> 00:18:27,140
as a... Kind of a thank

364
00:18:22,350 --> 00:18:27,140
you for being such a great roommate.

365
00:18:27,310 --> 00:18:30,770
I can't take the big, white dog. You love it.

366
00:18:31,190 --> 00:18:33,400
It's "him." Not "it."

367
00:18:34,360 --> 00:18:37,110
Well, what if I bought it from you, you know?

368
00:18:37,280 --> 00:18:40,450
And then your nice gesture would be giving it to me at a reasonable price.

369
00:18:40,610 --> 00:18:42,320
Say $1500?

370
00:18:44,200 --> 00:18:47,910
Wait a second. I see what you're trying to do here.

371
00:18:48,080 --> 00:18:50,290
You're trying to give me money again.

372
00:18:50,710 --> 00:18:52,460
When did I try to give you money?

373
00:18:52,630 --> 00:18:54,460
Before, over there with the bills.

374
00:18:54,630 --> 00:18:57,510
You tried to give me charity, I said no, you dropped it.

375
00:18:57,670 --> 00:18:59,800
Okay, then we had a nice last night together.

376
00:18:59,970 --> 00:19:03,550
We had some fun, we gambled, nobody tried to give anybody any money.

377
00:19:05,640 --> 00:19:08,560
Now, out of the blue, you start with the charity thing again.

378
00:19:08,730 --> 00:19:12,520
I'm just trying to help you out, okay? I wanna make sure that you're okay.

379
00:19:12,690 --> 00:19:14,810
I will be okay. Look, Chandler.

380
00:19:14,980 --> 00:19:18,990
You gotta get it out of your head that I can't take care of myself, okay?

381
00:19:19,530 --> 00:19:23,450
Look, I'm not gonna miss you helping me out with money.

382
00:19:23,620 --> 00:19:26,080
The only thing I'm gonna miss...

383
00:19:26,410 --> 00:19:28,080
is you.

384
00:19:30,620 --> 00:19:32,290
And now the dog.

385
00:19:39,260 --> 00:19:40,590
Hey.

386
00:19:41,340 --> 00:19:43,430
Call me when you get there, okay?

387
00:19:41,340 --> 00:19:43,430
Okay.

388
00:19:43,590 --> 00:19:45,390
I'm really gonna miss you.

389
00:19:51,980 --> 00:19:54,440
Oh, I have your key.

390
00:19:55,440 --> 00:19:58,020
Here you go.

391
00:19:55,440 --> 00:19:58,020
Thanks.

392
00:20:03,410 --> 00:20:07,660
Oh, God, this is silly. I'm gonna see you in a couple of hours.

393
00:20:09,080 --> 00:20:10,410
Bye, house.

394
00:20:15,960 --> 00:20:17,040
Bye

395
00:20:15,960 --> 00:20:17,040
bye.

396
00:20:15,960 --> 00:20:17,040
Bye.

397
00:20:40,280 --> 00:20:41,650
Hey.

398
00:20:42,690 --> 00:20:45,740
She really left.

399
00:20:42,690 --> 00:20:45,740
I know.

400
00:20:48,160 --> 00:20:51,660
Thank you.

401
00:20:48,160 --> 00:20:51,660
No problem, roomie.

402
00:20:59,340 --> 00:21:01,800
Can I ask you a question?

403
00:20:59,340 --> 00:21:01,800
Sure.

404
00:21:01,960 --> 00:21:04,510
What the hell is that dog doing here?

405
00:21:09,010 --> 00:21:12,310
I invented the game of Cups as a way to give Joey money.

406
00:21:12,470 --> 00:21:15,980
And now you want that money back?

407
00:21:12,470 --> 00:21:15,980
Exactly.

408
00:21:16,140 --> 00:21:18,520
Chandler, what kind of idiot do you take me for?

409
00:21:19,820 --> 00:21:21,900
It's not a real game. I made it up.

410
00:21:22,070 --> 00:21:25,240
I'm sorry you lost your money. But I won it fair and square.

411
00:21:25,400 --> 00:21:27,110
At a fake game!

412
00:21:27,860 --> 00:21:30,660
Now, if you wanna try to make some of it back...

413
00:21:30,830 --> 00:21:34,080
I'd be glad to play you for it. But I should warn you.

414
00:21:34,250 --> 00:21:37,710
I am very good at Cups.

415
00:21:38,420 --> 00:21:42,170
Okay, now, I assume the saucer card came up when you played last?

416
00:21:43,090 --> 00:21:44,300
No.

417
00:21:43,090 --> 00:21:44,300
Hmm.

418
00:21:44,460 --> 00:21:47,050
Let's see if it comes up this time.

